  "definition": "Image Processing is the computational manipulation of digital images using mathematical operations to enhance visual quality, extract information, or transform image representations for downstream analysis or display. It encompasses classical signal processing operations\u2014filtering, convolution, histogram equalisation, morphological operations, and frequency-domain transforms\u2014as well as learned operations implemented through convolutional neural networks and vision transformers. Image processing is a prerequisite step in computer vision pipelines, medical imaging workflows, satellite remote sensing, and industrial quality inspection systems, operating on pixel grids to produce processed images or structured outputs.",
